!!! HTTP status codes.
!!!
!!! A number, not a choice. A choice would be a closed set, and the status
!!! space is not closed: an application is entitled to answer 418, or 207, or
!!! a code registered after this file was written, and a framework that cannot
!!! carry one is a framework its users have to work around. The named
!!! constants below are a convenience over the number, never a restriction on it.

book nilweb.http.status

read nil.std.text

public constant status-ok as number is 200
public constant status-created as number is 201
public constant status-accepted as number is 202
public constant status-no-content as number is 204
public constant status-partial-content as number is 206
public constant status-moved-permanently as number is 301
public constant status-found as number is 302
public constant status-see-other as number is 303
public constant status-not-modified as number is 304
public constant status-temporary-redirect as number is 307
public constant status-permanent-redirect as number is 308
public constant status-bad-request as number is 400
public constant status-unauthorized as number is 401
public constant status-forbidden as number is 403
public constant status-not-found as number is 404
public constant status-method-not-allowed as number is 405
public constant status-not-acceptable as number is 406
public constant status-request-timeout as number is 408
public constant status-conflict as number is 409
public constant status-payload-too-large as number is 413
public constant status-uri-too-long as number is 414
public constant status-unsupported-media-type as number is 415
public constant status-range-not-satisfiable as number is 416
public constant status-unprocessable as number is 422
public constant status-too-many-requests as number is 429
public constant status-internal-error as number is 500
public constant status-not-implemented as number is 501
public constant status-bad-gateway as number is 502
public constant status-service-unavailable as number is 503
public constant status-gateway-timeout as number is 504
public constant status-version-not-supported as number is 505


!!! --- The reason phrase for the status line.
!!!
!!! A code with no registered phrase gets the class default rather than an
!!! empty one, because a status line must have a reason token and an unknown
!!! 4xx is still plainly a client error.

public reason-phrase receives code as number returns text begin paragraph
    give switch code
        case 200 then stop switching with "OK"
        case 201 then stop switching with "Created"
        case 202 then stop switching with "Accepted"
        case 204 then stop switching with "No Content"
        case 206 then stop switching with "Partial Content"
        case 301 then stop switching with "Moved Permanently"
        case 302 then stop switching with "Found"
        case 303 then stop switching with "See Other"
        case 304 then stop switching with "Not Modified"
        case 307 then stop switching with "Temporary Redirect"
        case 308 then stop switching with "Permanent Redirect"
        case 400 then stop switching with "Bad Request"
        case 401 then stop switching with "Unauthorized"
        case 403 then stop switching with "Forbidden"
        case 404 then stop switching with "Not Found"
        case 405 then stop switching with "Method Not Allowed"
        case 406 then stop switching with "Not Acceptable"
        case 408 then stop switching with "Request Timeout"
        case 409 then stop switching with "Conflict"
        case 413 then stop switching with "Payload Too Large"
        case 414 then stop switching with "URI Too Long"
        case 415 then stop switching with "Unsupported Media Type"
        case 416 then stop switching with "Range Not Satisfiable"
        case 422 then stop switching with "Unprocessable Content"
        case 429 then stop switching with "Too Many Requests"
        case 500 then stop switching with "Internal Server Error"
        case 501 then stop switching with "Not Implemented"
        case 502 then stop switching with "Bad Gateway"
        case 503 then stop switching with "Service Unavailable"
        case 504 then stop switching with "Gateway Timeout"
        case 505 then stop switching with "HTTP Version Not Supported"
        otherwise stop switching with (class-phrase with code being code)
    end switch
end paragraph


class-phrase receives code as number returns text begin paragraph
    when code is at least 100 and code is at most 199 then give "Information" end when
    when code is at least 200 and code is at most 299 then give "Success" end when
    when code is at least 300 and code is at most 399 then give "Redirection" end when
    when code is at least 400 and code is at most 499 then give "Client Error" end when
    when code is at least 500 and code is at most 599 then give "Server Error" end when
    give "Unknown"
end paragraph


!!! --- A response with this status carries no body, whatever the handler set.
!!! RFC 9110: 1xx, 204 and 304 have no content, and a message that sends one
!!! anyway is unparseable by the client.

public status-forbids-body receives code as number returns boolean begin paragraph
    give (code is at least 100 and code is at most 199) or code equals 204 or code equals 304
end paragraph


!!! --- Whether the code is one a handler should be allowed to send at all.
!!! Outside 100..599 is a programming error, caught here rather than on the wire.

public is-valid-status receives code as number returns boolean begin paragraph
    give code is at least 100 and code is at most 599
end paragraph


public is-redirect receives code as number returns boolean begin paragraph
    give code equals 301 or code equals 302 or code equals 303
        or code equals 307 or code equals 308
end paragraph


public is-error receives code as number returns boolean begin paragraph
    give code is at least 400
end paragraph


!!! --- A status code as its three digits.
!!! Written here rather than borrowed, so the status line never depends on a
!!! general number formatter being correct about negatives or widths.

public status-digits receives code as number returns text begin paragraph
    when not (is-valid-status with code being code) then
        give "500"
    end when
    value hundreds is code over 100
    value tens is (code remainder 100) over 10
    value ones is code remainder 10
    give (digit-text with digit being hundreds)
        plus (digit-text with digit being tens)
        plus (digit-text with digit being ones)
end paragraph


digit-text receives digit as number returns text begin paragraph
    give switch digit
        case 0 then stop switching with "0"
        case 1 then stop switching with "1"
        case 2 then stop switching with "2"
        case 3 then stop switching with "3"
        case 4 then stop switching with "4"
        case 5 then stop switching with "5"
        case 6 then stop switching with "6"
        case 7 then stop switching with "7"
        case 8 then stop switching with "8"
        otherwise stop switching with "9"
    end switch
end paragraph
